@page "/components/data"

<PageTitle>Calendar, chart, conversation — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Calendar, chart, conversation</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    The three families where shadcn leans hardest on a JavaScript library — react-day-picker,
    recharts, and its own AI primitives — and where the honest port is mostly a decision about
    which parts of that were doing real work.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Calendar</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    A <code>&lt;table&gt;</code>, because a calendar is one and every screen reader already knows
    how to read it. Each day is a real radio input, so choosing one posts and the browser supplies
    the arrow keys — no roving tabindex, no key handlers, no state. For picking a single date in a
    form, <code>DatePicker</code> is smaller still; this is for when the shape of the month is the
    information.
</p>
<Example Source="CalendarExample.razor"><CalendarExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Chart</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    <code>ChartContainer</code> upstream does two things: declares one custom property per series,
    so whatever draws and whatever labels read the same colour from one place, and carries a wall
    of <code>[&amp;_.recharts-*]</code> selectors for a library this port does not ship. The first
    is the useful half and it is what <code>&lt;Chart&gt;</code> keeps. What draws is yours — and
    a real charting library, when you need one, renders inside this and reads the same properties.
</p>
<Example Source="ChartExample.razor"><ChartExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Conversation</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Message, Bubble, Attachment, Marker and the scroller. The scroller follows the newest message
    only while you are already at the bottom — scroll up to read something and it stops, which is
    the behaviour every chat needs and most get wrong in one direction or the other.
    <code>overflow-anchor</code> does that half in CSS; the browser has had it since 2018.
</p>
<Example Source="ConversationExample.razor"><ConversationExample /></Example>
